<title>TANZANIA: Tanzania telecommunications employees suspended.</title>
<headline>Tanzania telecommunications employees suspended.</headline>
<dateline>DAR ES SALAAM 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tanzania's state-owned telecommunications company said on Thursday it had suspended five employees accused of embezzling some 180 million Tanzanian shillings.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Tanzania Telecommunications Company said the five, who worked in the finance department, were alleged to have set up bogus bank accounts to deposit customers' payments.</p>
<p>The spokesman said it was the first case of large-scale suspected fraud by company employees. The government says it is stepping up an anti-corruption campaign among civil servants.</p>
<p>($1=600 Tanzanian shillings)</p>
</text>
